# Title: Credential Manager Access By Uncommon Applications
# ID: 407aecb1-e762-4acf-8c7b-d087bcff3bb6
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-10-11
# Tags: attack.t1003, attack.credential-access
# Description: Detects suspicious processes based on name and location that access the windows credential manager and vault.
# Which can be a sign of credential stealing. Example case would be usage of mimikatz "dpapi::cred" function
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((FileName CONTAIN "\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Credentials\\" OR FileName CONTAIN "\\AppData\\Roaming\\Microsoft\\Credentials\\" OR FileName CONTAIN "\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Vault\\" OR FileName CONTAIN "\\ProgramData\\Microsoft\\Vault\\")) AND NOT (((Image = "C:\\Windows\\explorer.exe") OR ((Image="C:\\Program Files\\*" OR Image="C:\\Program Files (x86)\\*" OR Image="C:\\Windows\\system32\\*" OR Image="C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\*")))))
